<title>PERU: Peru's Credicorp Q3 net per share rises 15.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru's Credicorp Q3 net per share rises 15.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third quarter</p>
<p>Share - $0.52 vs $0.45</p>
<p>Net - $31.9 million vs $27.5 million.</p>
<p>Revs - $78.9 million vs $65.6 million.</p>
<p>	  January to September</p>
<p>Share - $1.47 vs $1.18</p>
<p>Net - $90.1 million vs $72.2 million.</p>
<p>Revs - $233.5 million vs $180.8 million.</p>
<p>NOTES: Credicorp Ltd is the country's largest provider of financial services.</p>
<p>The company calculates its net per share results based on 61.3 million shares in free circulation, ignoring a further 10.2 million shares held by its subsidiaries. Credicorp owns 90.1 percent of Peru's largest full-service bank, Banco de Credito del Peru SA , 75.8 percent of insurance company Pacifico-Peruano Suiza and all of the diversified financial services company Atlantic Security Holding Corp.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 222-2134</p>
